Step 1: Understanding Main Concepts

TypeScript's main concepts form the foundation of the language. Key areas include
type annotations, interfaces, classes, and modules.

Type Annotations
Type annotations in TypeScript allow developers to specify the data types of
variables, function parameters, and return values. This helps catch errors early in
development and improves code readability.
$

let age: number = 25;
function greet(name: string): string {

