Quick Guide

Modules in TypeScript help organize code into logical units, promoting better
maintainability and reusability. They support both internal and external modules.
$

// math.ts
export function add(a: number, b: number): number {
return a + b;
}
// main.ts
import { add } from './math';
console.log(add(2, 3));

