Step 2: Exploring Syntax and Semantics

TypeScript's syntax is largely compatible with JavaScript but includes additional
features to improve type safety.

Variable Declarations
In TypeScript, variables can be declared using let or const , with explicit type
annotations.
$

let count: number = 0;
const pi: number = 3.14;

Function Parameters and Return Types
Functions in TypeScript have explicit parameter types and return types, enhancing
code clarity and maintainability.
$

function multiply(a: number, b: number): number {
return a * b;

localhost:7000/api/research/report/rp-465b3fe28b00

4/13

7/3/26, 7:44 PM

Quick Guide

}

Control Structures
Control structures like if , for , and while statements in TypeScript follow the
same syntax as JavaScript but with added type safety.
$

let x: number = 10;
if (x > 5) {
console.log("Greater than 5");
} else if (x === 5) {
console.log("Equal to 5");
} else {
console.log("Less than 5");
}

5

Step 3: Delving into the Type System

TypeScript's type system is one of its most powerful features, providing robust
support for various data types and complex structures.

Primitive Types
Primitive types include number , string , boolean , null , undefined , and symbol .
$

let age: number = 25;
let name: string = "John";
let isStudent: boolean = true;

Object Types
Object types define the structure of objects, including properties and methods.
localhost:7000/api/research/report/rp-465b3fe28b00

5/13

7/3/26, 7:44 PM

$

Quick Guide

interface Person {
firstName: string;
lastName: string;
greet(): void;
}
const john: Person = {
firstName: "John",
lastName: "Doe",
greet() {
console.log("Hello, " + this.firstName);
}
};

Array Types
Array types in TypeScript specify the type of elements within an array.
$

let numbers: number[] = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];
let names: string[] = ["Alice", "Bob"];

Tuple Types
Tuple types allow arrays to have a fixed number of elements with specific types.
$

let person: [string, number] = ["John", 25];

Union and Intersection Types
Union types represent a value that can be one of several types, while intersection
types combine multiple types into one.
$

type StringOrNumber = string | number;
type Student = { name: string } & { age: number };

