Namespaces
Namespaces help organize code into logical units and prevent naming conflicts.
$

namespace MathOperations {
export function add(a: number, b: number): number {
return a + b;
}
export function subtract(a: number, b: number): number {
return a - b;
}
}
console.log(MathOperations.add(5, 3));

Enums
Enums in TypeScript provide a way to define named constants, making the code
more readable and maintainable.
$

enum Direction {
Up,
Down,
Left,
Right
}
function move(direction: Direction) {
switch (direction) {
case Direction.Up:
console.log("Moving up");
break;
case Direction.Down:
console.log("Moving down");

