Async/Await
Async/await syntax simplifies working with promises, making asynchronous code
more readable and easier to manage.
$

async function fetchData() {
const response = await fetch('[https://api.example.com/data'](https://api.example.com/
const data = await response.json();
console.log(data);
}
fetchData().catch(error => console.error(error));

