Step 5: Exploring Tools and Libraries

TypeScript integrates well with a wide range of tools and libraries, enhancing its
functionality and developer productivity.

Babel
Babel is a JavaScript compiler that allows developers to use the latest JavaScript
features in their code while ensuring compatibility with older environments.

localhost:7000/api/research/report/rp-465b3fe28b00

9/13

7/3/26, 7:44 PM

$

Quick Guide

npm install --save-dev @babel/core @babel/preset-typescript babel-loader

Webpack
Webpack is a module bundler for modern web applications, allowing developers to
manage and bundle assets like JavaScript, CSS, and images.
$

npm install --save-dev webpack webpack-cli typescript ts-loader

React
React is a popular front-end library for building user interfaces. TypeScript provides
type safety and better tooling support when working with React.
$

import React from 'react';
import ReactDOM from 'react-dom';
interface AppProps {
title: string;
}
class App extends React.Component<AppProps> {
render() {
return <h1>{this.props.title}</h1>;
}
}
ReactDOM.render(<App title="Hello, TypeScript!" />, document.getElementById('root'));

8

Step 6: Best Practices and Coding Standards

