7/3/26, 7:44 PM

Quick Guide

Writing clean, maintainable, and efficient TypeScript code requires following best
practices and coding standards.

Code Organization
Organize code into logical modules and follow a consistent file structure to improve
readability and maintainability.
$

// src/
// ├── components/
// │

└── Button.tsx

// ├── services/
// │

└── UserService.ts

// ├── types/
// │

└── User.ts

// └── App.tsx

Naming Conventions
Use meaningful and descriptive names for variables, functions, and classes to
improve code readability.
$

let firstName: string = "John";
function calculateTotal(items: number[]): number {
return items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + item, 0);
}

Error Handling
Implement proper error handling using try-catch blocks and throw custom errors
when necessary.
$

try {
let result = divide(10, 0);
} catch (error) {
console.error("Error:", error.message);

